WEBVTT

00:54.320 --> 00:56.560
OPEN

01:00.440 --> 01:05.440
SEVEN STAB WOUNDS INFLICTED

01:11.640 --> 01:15.560
CLOSED

01:29.880 --> 01:33.280
ROUGH STREET

01:56.520 --> 02:03.520
MY 2 CENTS

02:03.600 --> 02:08.680
A SERIES BY ZEROCALCARE

02:08.760 --> 02:09.880
Home. Sofa.

02:09.960 --> 02:12.320
Play Super Mario on Super Nintendo.

02:12.920 --> 02:15.440
I get emotional thinking
how happy I was as a kid

02:15.520 --> 02:18.280
to be able to play a video game

02:18.360 --> 02:21.480
without needing three degrees
and having to watch 700 hours

02:21.560 --> 02:23.640
of videos of puppets with dead fish eyes

02:23.720 --> 02:26.400
and take a minimum
two-month sabbatical from life.

02:27.760 --> 02:31.200
Mum'll be mad hearing this
because she always says…

02:31.280 --> 02:33.040
You never left the house!

02:33.120 --> 02:36.640
It stank of stale air
and your sweaty hormone stench!

02:36.720 --> 02:39.440
Your room stank
like Pavarotti's ball sack.

02:40.480 --> 02:42.960
But she's referring to a specific time.

02:43.040 --> 02:45.480
The time of Final Fantasy VII.

02:45.560 --> 02:47.800
I almost failed
my first year of secondary school.

02:47.880 --> 02:50.040
But in terms of emotions
and literary value,

02:50.120 --> 02:53.040
it was seven-nil compared
to the entire Italian syllabus.

02:53.120 --> 02:55.360
Even that damn hunchback, what's his name?

02:56.000 --> 02:56.880
Giacomo Leopardi.

02:56.960 --> 02:59.520
Darling, please, can't you go to Villa Ada

02:59.600 --> 03:02.280
and smoke joints outside
like Carmela's kids?

03:02.360 --> 03:04.200
I think the good weed has arrived.

03:04.280 --> 03:06.200
Mario will give you a good price!

03:07.360 --> 03:10.040
I have to create the Gold Chocobo first!

03:10.560 --> 03:13.960
While I'm savouring the memory
of that whirlwind of emotions…

03:14.040 --> 03:15.440
SARAH
VOICE NOTE

03:15.520 --> 03:17.000
…I get this message.

03:17.080 --> 03:19.000
Where are you? We said eight.

03:19.080 --> 03:20.800
Jeez! It's ten past eight.

03:20.880 --> 03:22.800
I lost track of time!

03:22.880 --> 03:26.200
These videos suck me
into a dark area of my soul,

03:26.280 --> 03:30.440
a malignant crevice
where time passes differently.

03:30.960 --> 03:34.400
I have to come up with some bullshit
to explain what I was doing.

03:34.480 --> 03:36.120
Don't get upset. No need.

03:36.200 --> 03:39.320
We go through these theatrics every day.
We can handle it.

03:39.400 --> 03:40.920
Firstly, don't lie.

03:41.000 --> 03:43.000
Bullshit always gets found out.

03:43.080 --> 03:46.000
Write, "I'm on my way.
Sorry, I've just left."

03:46.080 --> 03:49.080
But that's a lie.
I still need to take a shower.

03:49.160 --> 03:51.720
It doesn't matter if it's not true now.

03:51.800 --> 03:53.120
It will be true soon.

03:53.200 --> 03:55.040
We need to get the message out

03:55.120 --> 03:58.720
and then work to reduce the lag
between real life and what we say.

03:58.800 --> 04:00.280
-The what?
-Lag.

04:01.120 --> 04:02.080
What?

04:02.160 --> 04:04.400
But start doing something. Come on.

04:04.480 --> 04:06.560
Put some effort in.

04:06.640 --> 04:10.600
Lag is the time between
sending and receiving a message.

04:10.680 --> 04:12.720
The grey area where bullshitters move.

04:12.800 --> 04:14.040
-Hey!
-No man's land.

04:14.120 --> 04:16.360
Like between your balls and your arse.

04:41.200 --> 04:43.920
How long does it take?
You live five minutes away!

04:44.000 --> 04:45.680
Say you're looking for parking.

04:45.760 --> 04:46.960
Add some details,

04:47.040 --> 04:50.120
like you need to park well
because of the traffic wardens.

04:50.200 --> 04:51.040
Tell her that.

04:51.120 --> 04:54.320
Come on!
I'm leaving soon if you don't get here!

04:54.400 --> 04:56.440
She's pissed off, and she's got a point.

04:56.520 --> 04:58.080
What the fuck do I tell her?

04:58.160 --> 05:00.520
You have to be ruthless.
Don't play defence.

05:00.600 --> 05:03.600
Attack. You have to attack!

05:06.400 --> 05:07.560
Okay, tell her,

05:07.640 --> 05:10.360
"I'm here. But where are you?
I can't see you."

05:11.360 --> 05:13.720
Don't fuck with me. You're not here!

05:13.800 --> 05:16.840
This place is 20 square metres.
You can't get lost.

05:16.920 --> 05:18.320
It's that small?

05:18.400 --> 05:19.840
It's a café.

05:19.920 --> 05:23.880
Why didn't you say that before?
How can I work like this?

05:23.960 --> 05:25.400
That went badly.

05:25.480 --> 05:26.800
But we tried, right?

05:26.880 --> 05:28.920
Fortune failed us, not our valour.

05:29.000 --> 05:30.960
Go make an arse of yourself. Bye.

05:31.040 --> 05:32.240
I made a mistake.

05:32.320 --> 05:34.200
I went to a different café.

05:34.280 --> 05:36.800
How could you make a mistake?
It's your café!

05:36.880 --> 05:39.200
It's your café.

05:39.280 --> 05:43.080
I still can't get my head around it.
"My café" just doesn't sound right.

05:43.160 --> 05:45.760
I know there are idiots
out there thinking…

05:45.840 --> 05:47.480
Look at Zerocalcare!

05:47.560 --> 05:50.080
"I'm young and underemployed.
I tutor kids,

05:50.160 --> 05:52.360
tear along the dotted line."
And he opens a café!

05:52.440 --> 05:55.640
They're all the same.
Like that pimp with the Trillionaire club.

05:55.720 --> 05:57.520
Trillionaire club? You moron.

05:57.600 --> 05:59.000
Go see for yourself.

05:59.080 --> 06:01.160
It's a shithole
with three Salmonella stars.

06:01.240 --> 06:02.440
It's been five years.

06:02.520 --> 06:05.120
My bald spot's so big
you could land a drone on it.

06:05.200 --> 06:07.080
At least I put my two cents aside.

06:07.160 --> 06:09.200
Why else make two series for Netflix?

06:09.280 --> 06:12.840
That's what everyone who knows me thought,
and as a matter of fact…

06:18.880 --> 06:21.120
This is the calm
before I get screwed, right?

06:21.200 --> 06:23.400
Before you line your coffin
with banknotes,

06:23.480 --> 06:25.640
do you want to run the café with me?

06:25.720 --> 06:26.880
Wild Boar asked me.

06:27.480 --> 06:29.560
Why are you asking? Is it going to shit?

06:30.160 --> 06:31.480
No, it's staying afloat.

06:31.560 --> 06:35.120
But I'm on my own with a lot of expenses.
I could use a partner.

06:35.200 --> 06:36.960
You know what our friends are like.

06:37.040 --> 06:39.560
They're just screaming monkeys
drowning in debt.

06:39.640 --> 06:41.640
But not you, you know?

06:41.720 --> 06:42.920
I'm not messed up?

06:43.000 --> 06:44.680
You are, but with no debts.

06:44.760 --> 06:45.800
And I thought,

06:45.880 --> 06:47.800
I've known Wild Boar all my life.

06:47.880 --> 06:50.480
You can talk to him about anything.

06:50.560 --> 06:53.800
You can tell him about any problem.
Really, like…

06:53.880 --> 06:56.720
I never get into REM sleep.
I wake up every half hour!

06:56.800 --> 06:58.920
If I let go, does it pull to the right?

06:59.000 --> 07:02.240
Do you think the guy who kills Joker
is the real Joker?

07:02.320 --> 07:05.040
He reduces everything
to the lowest common denominator

07:05.120 --> 07:06.520
and gets to the point.

07:06.600 --> 07:08.680
Mate, you need to get laid!

07:11.840 --> 07:13.800
I asked my father about the café thing.

07:13.880 --> 07:16.480
I belong to that generation
where, even at 40,

07:16.560 --> 07:19.720
if you have to spend over 50 smackers,
you double-check.

07:19.800 --> 07:22.040
You know about this stuff.
Is this a stupid move?

07:22.120 --> 07:23.600
This applies to everything,

07:23.680 --> 07:26.480
from getting a mortgage
to filling up your car.

07:29.960 --> 07:32.640
They all seem like acts of hubris to me,

07:32.720 --> 07:35.000
like pure arrogance
in the face of the gods.

07:35.080 --> 07:38.160
Hey, a full tank costs €80. Are you crazy?

07:38.240 --> 07:42.480
It may last you a week, but who's to say
there'll be any roads left in a week?

07:42.560 --> 07:46.200
You never know,
I could turn at any moment.

07:46.280 --> 07:48.920
Put €10 in.
You can always do it again tomorrow.

07:51.560 --> 07:54.440
Our parents, on the other hand,
lived in that Mesozoic era

07:54.520 --> 07:56.440
when you were an adult at 20,

07:56.520 --> 07:59.320
managing responsibilities and money.

07:59.400 --> 08:00.880
They got good at it.

08:05.240 --> 08:07.200
But then they decided that our generation

08:07.280 --> 08:10.520
should only be paid in sweets
until we're 80. So here we are.

08:10.600 --> 08:13.200
Anyway, when I asked my dad,
I was sure he'd say no.

08:13.280 --> 08:16.280
He never trusts anything.
He thinks everyone's out to get him.

08:16.880 --> 08:18.080
They're scamming us.

08:18.160 --> 08:20.320
We need a notary to check the paperwork.

08:20.400 --> 08:23.320
A notary? But it's just something quick.

08:23.400 --> 08:25.880
Yeah, but there are no guarantees.

08:26.400 --> 08:27.520
You mustn't rush.

08:27.600 --> 08:31.000
Let's call Lino's brother.
He's an agronomist and surveyor.

08:31.080 --> 08:33.400
Okay, fine. I won't get the Norcia salami.

08:33.480 --> 08:36.000
Can I at least get the Pringles?
They're only €4!

08:36.080 --> 08:37.120
No, €8 for you.

08:37.200 --> 08:39.320
Do what you want. It's your money.

08:39.920 --> 08:41.680
But against all expectations, he says…

08:41.760 --> 08:44.000
I think you should take that share.

08:44.080 --> 08:45.640
I like that kid.

08:47.120 --> 08:48.080
Wild Boar?

08:48.160 --> 08:51.960
Yeah, even as a kid,
he had all those qualities you lack.

08:52.040 --> 08:54.000
What? Like his business sense?

08:54.080 --> 08:56.480
At least I can talk to him about pussy.

08:57.000 --> 08:59.520
Faced with this accurate assessment,
I said,

08:59.600 --> 09:01.680
"Okay, let's get a share of this café."

09:11.400 --> 09:12.400
You need to get laid!

09:14.680 --> 09:16.920
Listen. I'm gonna tell you why I called.

09:17.000 --> 09:18.960
Sorry, just one thing. Did you go in?

09:19.040 --> 09:21.640
Who's in there? The usual three losers?

09:21.720 --> 09:23.280
Dunno. I never go there.

09:23.360 --> 09:26.080
Stella and I go to bed early.
We don't go out any more.

09:26.160 --> 09:28.560
I saw that big guy.
He looks South American.

09:28.640 --> 09:29.720
Yeah, Carlito.

09:31.920 --> 09:33.720
He's Cuban. He's great.

09:33.800 --> 09:35.760
Even if he was a dick, we wouldn't know

09:35.840 --> 09:38.840
because he never says a word.
So, he's great anyway.

09:39.440 --> 09:41.440
He dresses well because he's a chauffeur.

09:41.520 --> 09:43.120
When he's off, he comes here.

09:44.000 --> 09:47.200
When nature gives you a body
like a killing machine,

09:47.280 --> 09:49.520
you think the guy's a bully, right?

09:49.600 --> 09:51.080
But he just does his own shit.

09:51.160 --> 09:53.360
Reads the sports paper
and ignores everyone.

09:53.440 --> 09:55.560
Yeah, him. Quite the hottie.

09:55.640 --> 09:58.840
Too bad I find dicks disgusting,
or I'd shag him.

09:59.360 --> 10:01.280
Is Wild Boar happy at least?

10:02.440 --> 10:04.160
Come. I don't want to talk here.

10:04.760 --> 10:07.240
I need to talk to you
about something sensitive.

10:07.320 --> 10:10.120
-I wanted to explain it to you before…
-Hi, Zero.

10:10.200 --> 10:11.200
Hey, Montini.

10:11.280 --> 10:13.400
That's another guy who's always here.

10:13.480 --> 10:16.280
He lives up there.
He went to our school, remember?

10:16.360 --> 10:19.320
I do. But I only talked to him
like twice in five years.

10:19.400 --> 10:23.520
You might think that's hyperbole,
but I think she's overestimating.

10:24.320 --> 10:28.000
My school had a very rigid caste system.

10:31.080 --> 10:32.600
They came from India to study it,

10:32.680 --> 10:35.600
to understand
how we had managed to perfect

10:35.680 --> 10:37.600
that model of social segregation.

10:37.680 --> 10:39.080
All those years,

10:39.160 --> 10:42.640
you could only talk to people
who were just as tragic as you.

10:42.720 --> 10:44.840
Even the caretakers would hit you

10:44.920 --> 10:46.720
if you talked to someone better.

10:46.800 --> 10:48.720
The impudent boy with dandruff

10:48.800 --> 10:51.480
has laid eyes on Miss Lavinia!

10:52.720 --> 10:55.360
He will feel the whip!

10:55.440 --> 10:58.400
And we were tragic.
We're talking about the '90s,

10:58.480 --> 11:00.840
when tragic people were really tragic!

11:00.920 --> 11:04.000
Cool people
would never have thought of saying,

11:05.000 --> 11:07.320
I'm just like Sheldon
from The Big Bang Theory!

11:07.400 --> 11:10.120
That's not true, you piece of shit!
You were popular!

11:10.200 --> 11:11.880
Like if a Ku Klux Klan member said…

11:11.960 --> 11:15.320
Ha! That plantation slave
is just like me when I was young!

11:16.200 --> 11:18.280
But as tragic as we were,

11:18.360 --> 11:22.800
no one reached
Montini's level of being a total reject!

11:25.200 --> 11:27.320
He was the target
of every bully's tyranny,

11:27.400 --> 11:31.240
of every arsehole
who got out the wrong side of bed.

11:31.320 --> 11:34.840
I wouldn't limit that to humans.
I'd extend it to the fauna and flora.

11:34.920 --> 11:38.640
Even the pigeons would always
shit on his head during break.

11:38.720 --> 11:41.440
It can't have been coincidence.
It was like a rule.

11:41.520 --> 11:44.400
Like a leader pigeon
would have a go at the others

11:44.480 --> 11:45.880
if they shat anywhere else.

11:45.960 --> 11:47.080
Hey, guys, please.

11:47.160 --> 11:50.080
Is it too much to ask
for you to aim for the toilet?

11:50.160 --> 11:52.040
I bring the kids here to eat,

11:52.120 --> 11:54.840
and we're always
having to slalom through your shit!

11:54.920 --> 11:58.360
Please, there's even a sign!
Shit on the toilet!

11:58.440 --> 12:00.920
Only the toilet was Montini!

12:01.000 --> 12:03.440
What's he doing now?
Did he find his niche?

12:03.520 --> 12:05.640
I felt so sorry for him at school!

12:05.720 --> 12:07.600
I think he's still messed up.

12:07.680 --> 12:09.600
He walks around alone with that dog.

12:09.680 --> 12:13.040
It's like a rat that wheezes.
Like my grandpa who has emphysema.

12:21.720 --> 12:23.760
Okay, now I can say why I told you…

12:23.840 --> 12:26.480
Wait! Jeez, what's up? Do you need to pee?

12:26.560 --> 12:27.840
Are you in a hurry?

12:29.480 --> 12:32.840
I needed to tell you about Wild Boar,
but not at the café.

12:32.920 --> 12:35.960
Then tell me. What's up with Wild Boar?

12:36.040 --> 12:38.320
I don't know. He's in trouble, Sarah.

12:38.400 --> 12:40.840
But I don't know how to ask him.

12:40.920 --> 12:42.520
What do you mean, in trouble?

12:42.600 --> 12:45.240
He's married with kids.
Is he still messing around?

12:45.320 --> 12:48.480
If it's about pussy,
I'll go slap him myself, okay?

12:48.560 --> 12:50.080
Money keeps going missing.

12:50.160 --> 12:52.480
-What do you mean?
-I don't know.

12:52.560 --> 12:55.240
When I check the accounts each month,
nothing adds up.

12:55.320 --> 12:58.840
It wasn't that much at first.
I thought he'd made a mistake.

12:58.920 --> 13:00.680
But it's getting embarrassing now.

13:00.760 --> 13:03.360
Now think about the size of the multiverse

13:03.440 --> 13:05.120
and all the twists of fate

13:05.200 --> 13:08.080
that brought us to this situation.

13:08.160 --> 13:10.960
Your head spins
thinking about all the possibilities.

13:11.040 --> 13:12.920
But we're talking about money

13:13.000 --> 13:15.560
that's going missing
in bigger and bigger chunks.

13:15.640 --> 13:17.200
That narrows it down.

13:17.280 --> 13:19.200
Then the fact that we're in Rome.

13:19.280 --> 13:22.080
That basically leaves
only one explanation.

13:22.160 --> 13:23.560
Okay, so he does coke.

13:23.640 --> 13:27.920
Well, I don't think he's donating it
to the church to build a well in Africa.

13:28.000 --> 13:30.040
We need to talk to him, then.

13:30.120 --> 13:32.280
Yeah, but I get embarrassed.

13:32.360 --> 13:33.720
He's a role model for me.

13:33.800 --> 13:36.200
It's not my place to lecture him.

13:36.280 --> 13:38.040
I want us to go together,

13:38.120 --> 13:41.440
so he knows that my problem
isn't money going missing.

13:41.520 --> 13:44.280
It's just that if he's in that state,
he needs help.

13:44.360 --> 13:47.240
Why didn't you call
so we could talk to him together?

13:47.320 --> 13:52.360
Well, I told Secco about it,
but then the incident happened. You know.

13:52.440 --> 13:55.280
Oh yeah, sure. Poor guy. Jeez.

13:55.360 --> 13:57.080
Yeah, poor guy.

13:57.960 --> 14:01.720
The other day, I walked past his house
and got a lump in my throat.

14:01.800 --> 14:04.280
I could feel that heavy atmosphere.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.920
-It's his fault too, though.
-Yeah.

14:12.000 --> 14:14.320
But you wouldn't wish that on anyone.

14:14.400 --> 14:16.920
Anyway, I ended up
not talking to Wild Boar.

14:18.040 --> 14:20.120
I'll come with you if you want.

14:20.200 --> 14:21.840
Maybe another time.

14:21.920 --> 14:24.920
I'm really tired.
I can't handle that conversation.

14:25.000 --> 14:27.080
Thanks. At least we could talk.

14:27.160 --> 14:28.800
I want an early night.

14:28.880 --> 14:31.720
I'm glad we talked. I really needed that.

14:31.800 --> 14:33.480
-But, Zero…
-Call you tomorrow?

14:33.560 --> 14:35.400
Maybe we can have dinner with Stella.

14:35.480 --> 14:37.680
You're such a self-centred fuckface!

14:37.760 --> 14:39.640
You did all the talking!

14:40.840 --> 14:43.200
I'm not gonna let you
call me self-centred!

14:43.280 --> 14:45.160
I think we had a nice chat.

14:45.240 --> 14:46.640
I felt good vibes.

14:46.720 --> 14:49.840
What vibes? Have you got even dumber?

14:49.920 --> 14:52.480
Remember that we're here
because I asked you.

14:52.560 --> 14:54.440
I need to tell you something important!

14:55.160 --> 14:57.360
HEY, MUPPET, CAN WE MEET?
IT'S IMPORTANT

14:58.160 --> 15:00.240
Oh, sorry. I didn't read that bit.

15:00.320 --> 15:03.800
I've developed a psychic blindness
for anything that might be a hassle.

15:03.880 --> 15:05.040
I just don't see it.

15:07.520 --> 15:08.640
Okay, so what's up?

15:08.720 --> 15:11.320
I wanted to ask you
something a bit sensitive.

15:11.400 --> 15:13.600
So, first of all, it's in two parts.

15:13.680 --> 15:16.600
In my head, when someone
is about to ask me something,

15:16.680 --> 15:19.920
the Grand Council
of my wisest neurons gathers

15:20.000 --> 15:21.840
to assess the situation.

15:21.920 --> 15:23.840
-How's the prostate, Master?
-So-so.

15:29.280 --> 15:31.520
It's here, guys! The request is upon us!

15:32.680 --> 15:33.720
What's part one?

15:33.800 --> 15:38.120
So, first of all, I'm going through
a bit of a rough patch with Stella.

15:38.200 --> 15:41.640
A rough patch.
Meaning you broke up for the 670th time?

15:41.720 --> 15:44.280
No. Right now we're together.

15:44.360 --> 15:47.200
We just had
a rough five minutes this morning.

15:47.280 --> 15:49.200
-I hate you!
-You've ruined my life!

15:49.800 --> 15:52.480
Nothing serious, but the trend is

15:52.560 --> 15:55.520
we break up on Friday,
delete each other's socials on Saturday,

15:55.600 --> 15:57.400
on Tuesday, I send her a romantic song,

15:57.480 --> 15:59.960
and on Wednesday,
we fuck to get back together.

16:00.880 --> 16:02.760
Wow, it's like a weather forecast.

16:02.840 --> 16:06.400
There's an app that tells you
all your fights day by day,

16:06.480 --> 16:08.800
like the one that helps you lose weight.

16:08.880 --> 16:10.600
Don't worry. It's not a hassle.

16:10.680 --> 16:11.800
Love troubles.

16:11.880 --> 16:14.600
-I repeat, love troubles.
-Open up, Ettore!

16:17.520 --> 16:19.680
But you've been like this for years.

16:19.760 --> 16:22.480
I thought this was
some sort of harmony for you.

16:23.080 --> 16:26.240
The thing is, a friend of mine
had a fight with her boyfriend,

16:26.320 --> 16:28.400
and she's asked if she can stay with me

16:28.480 --> 16:30.560
because things are bad at home.

16:30.640 --> 16:33.240
He's a piece of shit. I don't know him,

16:33.320 --> 16:35.800
but she's told me really bad things.

16:35.880 --> 16:37.280
He hit her.

16:37.360 --> 16:39.600
I can't leave her on the street,

16:39.680 --> 16:41.680
and I can't send her back to him.

16:41.760 --> 16:43.400
Long live Sarah! Hurrah!

16:43.480 --> 16:46.680
'Cause she's a jolly good fellow

16:46.760 --> 16:49.800
-You're great for taking her in, sister!
-That piece of shit!

16:49.880 --> 16:51.680
Where does he live? We'll get him!

16:51.760 --> 16:55.080
What a shitty situation. How is she?

16:55.160 --> 16:56.680
She's a total mess,

16:56.760 --> 17:00.920
but it's a bit complicated
at home with Stella these days, you know?

17:01.000 --> 17:03.040
Okay, but what's the connection?

17:03.120 --> 17:07.680
Well, this thing is gonna upset
a very delicate balance.

17:07.760 --> 17:10.680
And she needs a quiet place, right?

17:10.760 --> 17:12.880
What the fuck is she asking me?

17:12.960 --> 17:16.760
Eeny, meeny, miny, moe

17:17.280 --> 17:20.720
The castle's been breached!
We were foolish!

17:20.800 --> 17:22.680
Sound the alarm! I'm gonna piss myself.

17:23.160 --> 17:26.520
So, basically,
just for a few days, if you could…

17:26.600 --> 17:31.640
let her stay!

17:35.560 --> 17:36.880
You're a piece of shit.

17:36.960 --> 17:38.600
You're dumping this on me

17:38.680 --> 17:40.920
because you knew
I'd feel guilty, damn you!

17:41.000 --> 17:42.840
Yeah, I'll be honest. Yes.

17:42.920 --> 17:44.120
That's how it is.

17:44.200 --> 17:48.160
We don't talk to you directly,
but to your sense of guilt.

17:48.240 --> 17:49.600
We skip you altogether.

17:49.680 --> 17:51.840
Don't worry. I'll talk to him.

17:51.920 --> 17:54.480
He'll do what I say. He's a puppet.

17:54.560 --> 17:56.000
Think about her too.

17:56.080 --> 17:59.240
I can't let a stranger into my house.

17:59.320 --> 18:02.360
Wait, this is the second part.
It's a bit shorter.

18:02.440 --> 18:03.920
She's not a stranger.

18:04.000 --> 18:05.160
Hi, Zero.

18:07.040 --> 18:09.480
Has this smartarse dropped the bomb?

18:09.560 --> 18:11.200
Smeralda?

18:12.400 --> 18:15.240
-My nappies!
-Stay with me, Mario!

18:15.320 --> 18:17.440
Okay, guys. It's Smeralda.

18:17.520 --> 18:20.040
Gentlemen, it was a pleasure
working with you.

18:20.120 --> 18:21.160
Goodbye.

18:27.320 --> 18:28.840
Oh, he's in shock.

18:28.920 --> 18:30.960
Look, you don't have to say yes.

18:31.040 --> 18:33.520
I did tell Sarah it was a bit much.

18:33.600 --> 18:36.520
A bit much?
This arsehole has a huge house,

18:36.600 --> 18:38.520
with a room for his plastic alligator.

18:38.600 --> 18:41.600
Leave Rosario alone. He needs his space.

18:43.040 --> 18:43.960
I want to say…

18:44.040 --> 18:47.560
Let's swap houses for a few days.
You take mine, but you handle this.

18:47.640 --> 18:50.280
But I don't.
I know what Sarah and Stella are like.

18:50.360 --> 18:53.440
We went on a road trip,
and they were fighting after 20 minutes.

18:53.520 --> 18:55.040
I was looking out the window,

18:55.120 --> 18:58.880
and I thought if Shenron the Dragon
appeared from behind the hill

18:58.960 --> 19:00.680
and could grant me one wish,

19:00.760 --> 19:02.360
I'd want to be a worm,

19:02.440 --> 19:05.160
or an animal
that can't hear or see anything

19:05.240 --> 19:08.040
and only relate to the world
through touch.

19:08.560 --> 19:11.960
But I still had all my senses,
so I could hear them screaming.

19:12.040 --> 19:14.680
I was so embarrassed I wanted to vanish.

19:14.760 --> 19:18.280
I tried to act casual
and scrolled through my phone,

19:18.360 --> 19:19.520
but then it died.

19:19.600 --> 19:22.200
So I started looking
at the seams of the seats,

19:22.280 --> 19:25.800
pretending to be interested,
when I was actually thinking…

19:25.880 --> 19:28.840
How the fuck can you fight
in front of other people?

19:28.920 --> 19:31.680
I have nothing against people who fight

19:31.760 --> 19:34.040
if they do it at home and don't flaunt it

19:34.120 --> 19:37.040
in front of my inner child,
who doesn't want to see it.

19:37.120 --> 19:38.480
Plus, I'm very judgmental

19:38.560 --> 19:41.680
so I had to bite my tongue
to not tell Sarah…

19:41.760 --> 19:44.120
Did you hear what she said to you?
Jeez, answer her!

19:44.200 --> 19:46.280
You're gonna let her treat you like that?

19:46.360 --> 19:48.560
But then she turned around and said…

19:48.640 --> 19:51.760
Sorry you had to witness this.

19:52.280 --> 19:55.560
And honestly, I couldn't hold it in
any more, so I said…

19:56.080 --> 19:57.520
Oh, were you fighting?

19:57.600 --> 20:01.440
I wasn't listening at all.
I was absorbed in looking at this seam.

20:01.520 --> 20:04.800
Look, this is great Italian craftsmanship!

20:05.520 --> 20:08.000
So I would've spared Smeralda from that.

20:08.720 --> 20:11.040
This idiot didn't tell me it was you

20:11.120 --> 20:13.080
or I wouldn't have said all that.

20:13.720 --> 20:15.200
What the fuck's going on?

20:15.280 --> 20:18.720
I don't know what she's told you,
but I'm in a bit of a mess.

20:18.800 --> 20:21.040
I think I need a change of scenery.

20:22.640 --> 20:25.600
Weird. You've always been
such a level-headed person

20:25.680 --> 20:29.360
with surgical precision
when it comes to judging people.

20:29.440 --> 20:32.000
Can I just say
that sounds weird coming from you?

20:32.080 --> 20:35.840
You're not known for surrounding yourself
with stable people.

20:35.920 --> 20:38.600
-I don't understa…
-You're a diviner of cringe.

20:38.680 --> 20:41.200
You go looking for it with a stick.

20:42.200 --> 20:44.760
You're completely wrong.
I'm not fascinated…

20:44.840 --> 20:46.840
Shh, please. Let's move on.

20:46.920 --> 20:48.960
Or this episode will never fucking end.

20:49.040 --> 20:50.960
Oh, but I trust humanity.

20:51.040 --> 20:53.240
I like to bet
on people's hidden qualities.

20:53.320 --> 20:54.760
So, can we stay with you?

20:54.840 --> 20:57.320
I have other people waiting.
I don't need to beg.

20:57.400 --> 20:59.720
What do you mean, "we"?

20:59.800 --> 21:02.880
You and your 450 personalities?

21:02.960 --> 21:05.600
If you have a kid,
I swear I'll kill myself.

21:05.680 --> 21:07.320
Oh, didn't Sarah tell you?

21:08.920 --> 21:09.760
Schiocco!

21:19.080 --> 21:22.320
Sarah, for fuck's sake.
You're burdening me with a zoo.

21:22.400 --> 21:24.720
Oh, stop it. He's so good.

21:24.800 --> 21:27.600
Even the cats bullied him at my place.

21:27.680 --> 21:32.600
Right, Schiocco?
Submissive in a house full of women!

21:33.120 --> 21:35.120
So? What have you decided?

21:35.200 --> 21:36.760
What's there to decide?

21:36.840 --> 21:40.120
She's escaping from a guy who hits her.
You've known her forever.

21:40.200 --> 21:41.920
You even have a guest room.

21:42.000 --> 21:43.440
How can you say no?

21:43.520 --> 21:46.760
What did they teach you?
Your mother, father, Dragon Shiryu,

21:46.840 --> 21:50.240
Master Yoda, Ken the Warrior,
Nelson Mandela, Max Pezzali,

21:50.320 --> 21:53.120
all those who tried
to pass on two cents of values to you.

21:53.200 --> 21:55.760
They'd spit in your face
if you don't let her stay.

21:59.240 --> 22:01.480
So? What are we gonna do?

22:02.280 --> 22:04.080
But tomorrow, please.

22:04.160 --> 22:06.640
Let me have one last night as a free man.

22:08.680 --> 22:10.280
Thanks, Zero. For real.

22:10.880 --> 22:13.120
But how long are we talking about?

22:13.200 --> 22:16.120
Not long. I'll get the hell out
before you get tired of me!

22:16.200 --> 22:17.400
But I hope you don't.

22:17.480 --> 22:19.400
So, let's talk tomorrow,

22:19.480 --> 22:22.480
and we'll agree
on when I can deliver this package.

22:24.680 --> 22:28.040
I can't believe you still blush
like when you were 12!

22:28.120 --> 22:29.640
You're such an idiot!

22:34.080 --> 22:35.920
BYE, CATERPILLAR

22:37.680 --> 22:39.120
CRAZY PIZZA

22:51.200 --> 22:52.920
IF YOU LEAVE ME, BOO-HOO

23:29.200 --> 23:32.000
You know you didn't accept
purely out of guilt?

23:32.680 --> 23:35.200
It's only because
she's in a shitty situation.

23:35.280 --> 23:36.280
You're a liar.

23:36.360 --> 23:39.320
Worse than a Jesuit.
A silo full of Jesuits.

23:39.400 --> 23:41.680
What else could I say?
She was right there!

23:41.760 --> 23:43.600
I'm not judging. Not saying anything.

23:43.680 --> 23:47.040
Just don't give me grief later,
or I'll make you pay.

23:49.080 --> 23:51.440
Did you notice
in your pantheon of role models,

23:51.520 --> 23:54.160
apart from your mother, they're all men?

23:54.960 --> 23:58.920
I think Netflix will send you
to a re-education camp in Siberia.

24:02.160 --> 24:04.520
So what? I was born in the '80s.

24:04.600 --> 24:08.640
There was no Eleven,
no Handmaid's Tale, all that cool stuff.

24:08.720 --> 24:11.920
All the girls in cartoons
were dainty little crybabies.

24:12.000 --> 24:13.360
No fucking role models.

24:14.520 --> 24:16.560
And what about the French girl?

24:24.720 --> 24:26.280
Toxic male.

24:27.280 --> 24:28.960
Oh, how I cried.

24:29.040 --> 24:32.400
I cried so much
when André banged her by the Seine.

24:32.480 --> 24:34.120
I couldn't sleep for days.

24:43.680 --> 24:45.160
Mate! Where were you?

24:45.240 --> 24:47.480
Smeralda was looking for you earlier!

24:47.560 --> 24:49.120
I ran into her outside.

24:49.200 --> 24:51.920
-She's going to stay with you?
-What can I do?

24:52.000 --> 24:54.480
Maybe this time
you'll finally get it done.

24:54.560 --> 24:58.520
Make me happy after 20 years.
What did I send you to school for?

24:58.600 --> 25:02.240
Forget it. She's not coming on holiday.
She's got problems.

25:02.320 --> 25:04.280
So what? In the history of humanity,

25:04.360 --> 25:06.880
has anyone stopped having sex
because they had problems?

25:06.960 --> 25:08.480
Look at the baby boom.

25:09.080 --> 25:10.280
I look at him and think,

25:10.360 --> 25:13.000
"You bastard. You're still screwing around

25:13.080 --> 25:14.920
instead of saying what you're up to."

25:15.000 --> 25:19.200
You pull that face because you think
I'm a country bumpkin from Sulmona.

25:19.280 --> 25:22.240
But it's not me saying it.
History says so!

25:22.320 --> 25:24.520
My grandfather's uncle lived by the coast

25:24.600 --> 25:26.960
when the Normans were raiding.

25:27.040 --> 25:28.440
Know what his dad told him?

25:28.520 --> 25:29.920
The dates don't match.

25:30.000 --> 25:33.760
My son, I understand
you're worried about the Normans,

25:33.840 --> 25:37.240
but the dog will take care of it.
He'll bark if he sees them.

25:38.680 --> 25:40.080
You only have to do one thing.

25:40.160 --> 25:41.800
You need to get laid!

25:43.360 --> 25:44.920
See why I can't talk to him?

25:45.000 --> 25:48.080
I can't say, "Sit down,
and let's talk about your problem."

25:48.160 --> 25:50.040
Because he's always been like that.

25:50.120 --> 25:52.040
You might think he's an arsehole,

25:52.120 --> 25:55.120
but he was the arsehole
who knew more than anyone else.

25:55.200 --> 25:59.120
He gave you advice because
he had more experience than you.

25:59.200 --> 26:03.520
The things that make you
the alpha male in the male hierarchy.

26:04.200 --> 26:07.840
Remember what I said
about the caste system at my school?

26:07.920 --> 26:09.000
Well,

26:09.840 --> 26:14.400
Wild Boar was the only one who
could switch from one caste to another.

26:17.600 --> 26:19.760
He'd hang out with us tragic guys,

26:19.840 --> 26:21.920
then he'd go out with Monica,

26:22.000 --> 26:24.720
who was at the top of the social pyramid.

26:24.800 --> 26:26.880
Before dinner, he'd come back to us

26:26.960 --> 26:30.760
and tell us how shiny the world above was.

26:30.840 --> 26:35.240
He was like the Dune Messiah,
who could walk between two worlds.

26:35.320 --> 26:38.600
Lisan al-Gaib!

26:40.360 --> 26:42.280
Even when he married Christine,

26:42.360 --> 26:44.960
it didn't seem like he was settling down.

26:48.360 --> 26:52.360
No, he'd look down on you, as if to say…

26:52.440 --> 26:55.960
You guys are just kids.
I'll explain when you grow up.

26:56.840 --> 26:58.720
The thing is, after all these years

26:58.800 --> 27:01.800
of him being the messiah
and us being the disciples,

27:01.880 --> 27:03.280
how can you one day say…

27:03.360 --> 27:04.800
Hey, bro, that's enough.

27:04.880 --> 27:07.640
You were good at getting laid,
but now you're desperate.

27:07.720 --> 27:09.800
You're hooked on this stuff,

27:09.880 --> 27:11.720
and now we have to help you.

27:11.800 --> 27:14.800
We, the tragic guys
who hung on your every word!

27:14.880 --> 27:16.600
It's humiliating for him.

27:16.680 --> 27:19.080
And we'd have to throw away this script

27:19.160 --> 27:22.040
and stop playing these roles
we've always played.

27:22.120 --> 27:23.680
And that scares me.

27:23.760 --> 27:26.880
I don't know how to live
without someone to reassure me

27:26.960 --> 27:28.720
and tell me I'm doing okay.

27:39.760 --> 27:42.360
If we step out of the comfort zone
of this little theatre,

27:42.440 --> 27:45.000
of us being here on this lit stage,

27:45.080 --> 27:49.000
I don't know what's out there.
It's all dark. You can't see anything.

28:12.360 --> 28:13.920
I don't know where we're going.

28:14.680 --> 28:15.920
I'm blind.

28:19.240 --> 28:22.080
But it's not a problem
because suddenly he tells me…

28:22.160 --> 28:24.440
You didn't see me tonight.
I'll explain later.

28:24.520 --> 28:25.600
What do you mean?

28:25.680 --> 28:27.160
I'll explain later!

28:27.800 --> 28:30.640
I didn't understand.
He seemed like a complete idiot,

28:30.720 --> 28:33.240
until I heard that bell.

28:40.760 --> 28:41.880
Good evening.

28:45.560 --> 28:46.720
Carlito.

28:51.840 --> 28:52.880
Miss.

29:04.400 --> 29:05.640
Do we know each other?

29:05.720 --> 29:07.920
Of course we know each other!

29:08.000 --> 29:09.640
You're Moody!

29:10.480 --> 29:11.640
MOODY

29:12.240 --> 29:14.040
Expert in Japanese katana,

29:14.120 --> 29:15.840
highly esteemed cocaine addict,

29:15.920 --> 29:18.760
and champion of what
no one called bullying at the time,

29:18.840 --> 29:23.080
just "I'll beat you to a pulp.
You know why? Because I can!"

29:23.160 --> 29:25.120
We all sucked it up because in the '80s,

29:25.200 --> 29:27.920
the greatest luminary
of developmental psychology

29:28.000 --> 29:29.440
was Charles Darwin.

29:29.520 --> 29:31.520
NATURAL SELECTION
MONTESSORI SUCK IT

29:31.600 --> 29:33.920
For decades,
he was the terror of East Rome.

29:34.000 --> 29:37.160
He doesn't remember us
because we were all potential victims.

29:37.240 --> 29:40.040
Practically everyone
in his field of vision

29:40.120 --> 29:41.760
was a potential victim.

29:41.840 --> 29:44.320
A bit less now,
since he moved to Dicksville

29:44.400 --> 29:45.640
due to a promotion.

29:45.720 --> 29:48.520
And it's not a career
where you can work from home.

29:52.240 --> 29:54.200
I don't think we know each other.

29:55.560 --> 29:57.880
Okay, I was looking for the hog.

29:57.960 --> 29:59.320
He's not here tonight.

30:00.480 --> 30:02.880
And this place stays open on its own?

30:03.520 --> 30:05.200
I'm here. I'm his friend.

30:05.280 --> 30:06.720
You can leave a message.

30:09.640 --> 30:12.200
I don't have to tell him anything.
Don't worry.

30:12.280 --> 30:15.880
Mind if I look at the kitchen?
I want to open a café too.

30:15.960 --> 30:17.440
You can't go in there.

30:17.520 --> 30:19.200
Thanks. I'll be quick.

30:30.960 --> 30:33.200
So, the hog isn't working today.

30:33.280 --> 30:35.280
No, he's not here much these days.

30:35.360 --> 30:36.800
Not sure when he'll be back.

30:36.880 --> 30:38.560
He doesn't like to do shit, huh?

30:38.640 --> 30:40.400
No, he actually works a lot.

30:40.480 --> 30:41.720
It's just recently…

30:41.800 --> 30:44.960
It's not good when
your friend doesn't like to do shit.

30:46.400 --> 30:49.400
Because his problems become your problems.

30:49.480 --> 30:51.280
Yeah,

30:51.360 --> 30:52.880
it's really not good.

30:52.960 --> 30:54.480
I'm sorry, what problems?

30:58.240 --> 30:59.920
Anyway, have a nice evening.

31:01.360 --> 31:04.520
I'll tell him you stopped by.
What's your name?

31:07.120 --> 31:08.240
No names.

31:08.320 --> 31:10.320
Tell him Dicksville stopped by.

31:11.360 --> 31:13.600
Hey, you! Give me a lift home?

31:13.680 --> 31:16.920
-You were leaving, right?
-But I live right here.

31:17.000 --> 31:19.640
You can take a ride. Buy some cigarettes.

31:19.720 --> 31:21.880
But my car's parked far away.

31:21.960 --> 31:24.000
Go get it. I'll wait here.

31:27.960 --> 31:29.200
I live right here!

32:08.160 --> 32:10.040
Come out. Jeez!

32:10.800 --> 32:13.520
What the fuck are you up to?

32:14.400 --> 32:16.440
Don't tell Christine anything!

32:19.800 --> 32:24.720
GOODBYE LORENZO
2004-2025

35:19.760 --> 35:22.120
Subtitle translation by: Adam Dean
